Give the BSDs a server directory, a user profile directory, a desktop name
and a physical memory size.

Five places in system_util.cc name Windows, macOS, Linux and WASM and stop
otherwise.  Two of them say so in a comment ("the compiler raises an error
because of no return value"), and the user profile directory ends in
"#error Undefined target platform."

GetDesktopNameAsString() and GetTotalPhysicalMemory() are the quieter pair:
falling off the end of a function returning non-void is a warning, not an
error, so on the BSDs they compiled and returned whatever happened to be in
the register.  The DISPLAY variable and sysconf(_SC_PHYS_PAGES) are what the
BSDs use too, so they take the Linux arms.

The BSDs install the server where Linux does and follow the same XDG layout
for the profile, so they take those arms as well.

This is the 3.33.6089 shape of part of the first commit on zakinko/mozc
bsd-support, where master needs if constexpr instead.  CI only.

